---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Capabilities', href: '/#capabilities' },
  { name: 'Data Engineering', href: '' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Data Engineering Services | Substrate"
  description="Substrate helps enterprises design, build, modernize, and operate data platforms. Reliable data pipelines, robust architecture, and trusted insights at scale."
>
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 1. HERO -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section class="relative overflow-hidden py-24 md:py-40" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_right,_var(--c-accent-soft)_0%,_transparent_60%)] pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true" />
  <div class="container-x relative z-10">
    <nav class="mb-10 text-sm text-ink-3">
      {breadcrumbs.map((crumb, idx) => (
        <span>
          {idx > 0 && ' / '}
          {crumb.href && idx < breadcrumbs.length - 1
            ? <a href={crumb.href} class="text-accent hover:underline">{crumb.name}</a>
            : <span class={idx === breadcrumbs.length - 1 ? 'font-medium text-ink' : ''}>{crumb.name}</span>
          }
        </span>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <div class="max-w-4xl" data-reveal-group>
      <p class="kicker text-accent mb-5" data-reveal>
        <span class="text-accent">01</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;—&nbsp;</span>Data Engineering
      </p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading" class="display text-5xl md:text-[4.5rem] text-ink max-w-5xl" data-reveal>
        Reliable data platforms.<br />Trusted insights at scale.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg md:text-xl text-ink-2 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed" data-reveal>
        Data engineering is the foundation of every data-driven organization. Substrate helps enterprises design, build, and operate robust data platforms that transform raw data into trusted, actionable insights.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4" data-reveal>
        <Button href="/contact" variant="primary" size="md">Talk to our team</Button>
        <Button href="#what-is" variant="secondary" size="md">Learn more</Button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 max-w-4xl" data-reveal-group>
      <div class="border-t border-line pt-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-3xl font-display font-semibold text-accent">70%</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mt-1">Enterprise data sits unused — locked in silos, unprocessed, or inaccessible to decision-makers</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t border-line pt-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-3xl font-display font-semibold text-accent">3-5x</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mt-1">Faster time-to-insight with modern data pipelines and automated dataOps practices</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t border-line pt-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-3xl font-display font-semibold text-accent">40%</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mt-1">Average infrastructure cost reduction through modern data architecture and optimization</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 2. WHAT IS DATA ENGINEERING? -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section id="what-is" class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-graphite" aria-labelledby="whatis-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="whatis-heading"
      index="02"
      label="What is Data Engineering"
      title="The discipline of turning raw data into reliable, production-grade systems."
      lede="Data engineering is the practice of designing, building, and maintaining the infrastructure and pipelines that collect, store, process, and make data available for analysis, machine learning, and operational use cases. It is the engineering backbone of every data-driven organization."
      tone="graphite"
    />

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16" data-reveal-group>
      <div data-reveal>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-4">Definition and scope</h3>
        <p class="text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Data engineering encompasses the entire lifecycle of data: ingestion from source systems, transformation and cleaning, storage in optimized formats, orchestration of pipelines, and delivery to consumers. It includes the platforms, tools, and processes that make data reliable, accessible, and governable at scale.
        </p>
        <p class="text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
          A well-engineered data platform abstracts the complexity of underlying infrastructure, enforces data quality and governance, and provides self-service access to data consumers across the organization. It is the difference between a data swamp and a data asset.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-4">Why it matters for business</h3>
        <p class="text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Organizations invest in data engineering to unlock the value of their data assets. Without robust data engineering, analytics is built on fragile foundations, machine learning models train on unreliable data, and operational decisions are made without accurate information.
        </p>
        <p class="text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
          Companies that invest in modern data engineering practices report faster time-to-insight, higher trust in data, lower total cost of ownership, and the ability to scale data operations without proportionally scaling headcount.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-4">Data engineering vs. data science vs. analytics</h3>
        <p class="text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Data engineering builds the infrastructure and pipelines. Data science explores and models data to generate predictions and insights. Analytics consumes data through reports, dashboards, and ad hoc queries. All three are essential, but data engineering is the foundation upon which the others depend.
        </p>
        <p class="text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
          Without strong data engineering, data scientists spend 80% of their time cleaning and preparing data. With it, they focus on creating value. The best data organizations invest in engineering first and science second.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-4">Common misconceptions</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-graphite-fg-2">
            <span class="block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-bright mt-2 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span><strong class="text-graphite-fg">Data engineering is not just ETL.</strong> Modern data engineering includes streaming, real-time processing, dataOps, data governance, and platform engineering.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-graphite-fg-2">
            <span class="block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-bright mt-2 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span><strong class="text-graphite-fg">It is not only for big data.</strong> Organizations of all sizes benefit from systematic data engineering. Scale matters, but so does reliability and quality.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-graphite-fg-2">
            <span class="block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-bright mt-2 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span><strong class="text-graphite-fg">A data warehouse is not a data platform.</strong> Warehouses are components. A data platform includes ingestion, transformation, orchestration, governance, cataloging, and delivery.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-graphite-fg-2">
            <span class="block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-bright mt-2 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span><strong class="text-graphite-fg">Cloud does not solve data engineering automatically.</strong> Lift-and-shift to the cloud without rearchitecting data pipelines replicates existing problems at higher cost.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 3. BUSINESS CHALLENGES -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28" aria-labelledby="challenges-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="challenges-heading"
      index="03"
      label="Business Challenges"
      title="The cost of fragmented, unreliable data infrastructure."
      lede="Organizations that neglect data engineering accumulate technical debt, data quality issues, and operational overhead that prevent them from becoming truly data-driven."
    />

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" data-reveal-group>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">01</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Data silos</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data is scattered across departments, systems, and formats. No single source of truth exists. Business users cannot get a complete view of operations or customers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">02</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Poor data quality</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Duplicate records, missing values, inconsistent formats, and outdated data erode trust. Decisions are made on bad data, leading to wrong outcomes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">03</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Legacy ETL complexity</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Ancient ETL jobs running on fragile infrastructure. Scheduled batch windows, hard-coded transformations, and unmaintained code that no one wants to touch.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">04</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Slow reporting</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Dashboards and reports take days or weeks to build. Data refreshes are slow. Business users cannot get answers to urgent questions in real time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">05</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Fragmented systems</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data warehouses, lakes, operational databases, and analytics tools exist in isolation. No unified data mesh or fabric connects them coherently.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">06</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Scaling challenges</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data volumes grow exponentially. Existing pipelines cannot keep up. Infrastructure costs spiral as manual scaling and over-provisioning become the norm.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">07</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">High infrastructure costs</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Over-provisioned compute, orphaned storage, and inefficient query patterns drive cloud data costs higher than necessary without clear allocation or governance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">08</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Data governance gaps</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">No clear ownership, lineage tracking, or metadata management. Compliance audits are painful. Data cataloging is manual or nonexistent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">09</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Security and compliance</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">PII, sensitive data, and regulated data are not properly classified, encrypted, or access-controlled. GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, and SOC 2 compliance is at risk.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">10</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Lack of real-time data</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Batch processing is the only option. Business decisions are made on data that is hours or days old. Real-time streaming capabilities are absent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">11</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Manual data processing</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data pipelines require manual intervention to run, monitor, and fix. DataOps maturity is low. Pipeline failures go undetected for hours or days.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">12</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Integration complexity</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Connecting SaaS applications, on-premises databases, APIs, and external data sources requires custom integration work that is fragile and hard to maintain.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 4. DATA ENGINEERING APPROACH -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-graphite" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="approach-heading"
      index="04"
      label="Our Approach"
      title="A systematic methodology for modern data platforms."
      lede="We follow a structured, outcome-driven approach that meets you where you are. From legacy ETL to modern event-driven architectures, every phase is tailored to your data maturity and business goals."
      tone="graphite"
    />

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" data-reveal-group>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">01</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Discovery</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Map existing data landscape: sources, pipelines, storage, consumers, pain points, and business objectives. We produce a comprehensive data maturity assessment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">02</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Assessment</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Deep analysis of data quality, pipeline reliability, infrastructure cost, governance maturity, and team capabilities. Prioritized remediation roadmap delivered.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">03</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Strategy</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Define the target data architecture, technology stack, migration approach, and adoption roadmap. Aligned with business priorities and budget constraints.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">04</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Architecture Design</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Design the data platform architecture: ingestion layer, storage, processing, orchestration, catalog, governance, and consumption interfaces. Blueprints and decision logs delivered.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">05</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Data Modeling</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Design logical and physical data models optimized for query performance, storage efficiency, and business semantics. Dimensional, data vault, and lakehouse modeling.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">06</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Pipeline Design</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Design data pipelines for batch and streaming workloads. Error handling, retry logic, idempotency, and monitoring built into every pipeline from day one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">07</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Platform Engineering</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Build the data platform foundation: infrastructure as code, CI/CD for data, self-service environments, and automated provisioning for data teams.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">08</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Data Governance</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Implement governance frameworks: data catalog, lineage tracking, ownership, access controls, retention policies, and compliance automation from the start.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">09</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Data Quality</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Establish data quality frameworks: validation rules, profiling, monitoring dashboards, alerting, and remediation workflows. Trusted data as a service.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">10</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Data Security</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Implement data security: encryption at rest and in transit, row-level security, dynamic data masking, PII detection, and audit logging for compliance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">11</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Automation</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Automate everything: data ingestion, transformation, testing, deployment, monitoring, and incident response. DataOps practices eliminate manual toil.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">12</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Monitoring</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Comprehensive data observability: pipeline health, data freshness, volume trends, schema changes, and quality metrics. Proactive alerting prevents data incidents.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <span class="block font-mono text-xs text-accent-bright mb-3">13</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Continuous Optimization</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Data platforms are never finished. Establish cost governance, performance tuning, reliability reviews, and maturity tracking to drive ongoing improvement.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 5. DATA ENGINEERING SERVICES -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28" aria-labelledby="services-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="services-heading"
      index="05"
      label="Our Services"
      title="End-to-end data engineering capabilities."
      lede="From strategy through managed operations, we provide the full range of services needed to design, build, and run enterprise data platforms at scale."
    />

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" data-reveal-group>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-7" data-reveal>
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mb-3">SERVICE</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-display font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Data Strategy &amp; Consulting</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">Define your data vision, target architecture, technology stack, and multi-year roadmap aligned with business outcomes and data maturity.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-3"><span class="block h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" /> Current state assessment</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-3"><span class="block h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" /> Data maturity model</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-3"><span class="block h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" /> Phased implementation roadmap</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-7" data-reveal>
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mb-3">SERVICE</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-display font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Platform Engineering</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">Build the data platform foundation: infrastructure as code, automated provisioning, self-service environments, and CI/CD pipelines for data teams.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-3"><span class="block h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" /> Data platform architecture</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-3"><span class="block h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" /> IaC for data infrastructure</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-3"><span class="block h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" /> Self-service data environments</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-7" data-reveal>
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mb-3">SERVICE</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-display font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Data Architecture</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">Design modern data architectures: data mesh, data fabric, lakehouse, or cloud-native warehouse. Scalable, cost-effective, and fit for purpose.</p>
