<!-- 13. FAQ -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="faq-heading"
      index="13"
      label="Frequently Asked Questions"
      title="Common questions about data engineering."
      lede="Answers to the questions we hear most often from engineering leaders evaluating data platform investments."
    />

    <div class="mt-14 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4" data-reveal-group>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is the difference between a data lake and a data warehouse?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">A data lake stores raw data in native format on object storage. A data warehouse stores processed structured data optimized for analytics. Modern lakehouse architectures combine both: lake storage with warehouse-quality performance and ACID transactions.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How long does it take to build a modern data platform?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">A functional data platform with core pipelines can be delivered in 8 to 12 weeks. A mature platform with broad adoption, governance, and self-service capabilities typically takes 6 to 18 months. We prioritize early value.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          Do I need both a data lake and a data warehouse?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Not necessarily. A lakehouse architecture like Delta Lake or Apache Iceberg with an engine like Databricks or Trino can serve both raw data exploration and structured analytics from a single copy of data.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is data mesh and should we adopt it?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data mesh is an organizational pattern where domain teams own their data as products. It works well for large organizations with autonomous teams. For smaller organizations, a data fabric or lakehouse may be more practical.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you ensure data quality in production?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Through automated validation at every stage: schema validation at ingestion, quality checks in transformations, profiling and monitoring dashboards, and proactive alerting. Data contracts between producers and consumers maintain trust.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is the difference between batch and stream processing?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Batch processes data in scheduled intervals for large-scale transformations. Stream processes data continuously as it arrives for real-time analytics. Modern platforms combine both: batch for historical, streaming for real-time.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you handle PII and sensitive data?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">PII is detected through automated classification, encrypted at rest and in transit, and access-controlled through row-level security and dynamic data masking. Retention policies and audit logging ensure regulatory compliance.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is dataOps and why does it matter?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">DataOps applies DevOps to data: CI/CD for pipelines, automated testing, monitoring, and incident response. It reduces pipeline failures, improves data quality, and accelerates data product delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you choose between ETL and ELT?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">ETL transforms before loading, useful when targets have limited processing. ELT loads raw data first and transforms using warehouse compute. Modern platforms favor ELT for flexibility, scalability, and the ability to reprocess data.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          Can we migrate our legacy data warehouse to the cloud?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Yes. We have extensive experience migrating from Teradata, Oracle, Netezza, and on-premises SQL Server to Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, and Databricks with parallel run validation and minimal downtime.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is data lineage and why is it important?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data lineage tracks the origin, transformation, and movement of data through pipelines. It is essential for impact analysis, root cause investigation, compliance audits, and building trust in data.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you handle real-time data processing?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">We architect real-time pipelines using Apache Kafka or Kinesis for event transport, Flink or Kafka Streams for stream processing, and real-time sinks for analytics, databases, or APIs. Event-time processing and exactly-once semantics are standard.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is the typical ROI for data engineering investments?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Most organizations see measurable returns within 3 to 6 months: reduced pipeline failures, lower infrastructure costs, and faster report delivery. Full ROI including productivity gains and data trust materializes within 12 to 18 months.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you ensure data platform security?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Security is built into every layer: encryption at rest and in transit, row-level and column-level access controls, dynamic data masking, PII detection and classification, audit logging, and policy as code for compliance automation.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What is a data contract and why use it?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">A data contract is a formal agreement between data producers and consumers defining schema, quality SLAs, freshness expectations, and ownership. It prevents breaking changes and ensures trust across the data ecosystem.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you manage data platform costs?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">We implement cost governance through resource tagging, budget alerts, auto-scaling policies, right-sizing recommendations, query optimization, and scheduled shutdowns for non-production environments. FinOps practices ensure cost visibility.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          Can we adopt data engineering practices incrementally?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Yes. Data platform modernization is incremental. Start with a single data domain, a critical reporting use case, or a migration pilot. We prioritize early wins and build organizational confidence before scaling.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          What happens after the engagement ends?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Your team is equipped to operate and evolve the platform independently. We provide comprehensive documentation, runbooks, and training. Ongoing support and advisory retainers are available for continued access to our expertise.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-ink list-none">
          How do you measure data platform success?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-ink-2 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">We track data freshness, pipeline reliability, data quality scores, query performance, infrastructure cost per workload, platform adoption rate, data consumer satisfaction, and time from data generation to insight.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

